A variadic method on an interface provider: the receiver is the bare interface
value (no &/*), and the trailing slice argument forwards with the ... spread
(reporter.Report(options...)). The interface and the options have no producer,
so both become injector inputs.
-- config --
import-path: example.com/app
package-name: app
output: plumb_gen.go
-- example.com/app/app.go --
package app

type Option struct{}
type Summary struct{}

type Reporter interface {
	//plumb:build
	Report(opts ...Option) *Summary
}

//plumb:build
func Use(s *Summary) int { return 0 }
